      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most significant weakness in the UBI argument is the astronomical cost, which would necessitate massive tax hikes or unsustainable national debt. Opponents can devastatingly argue that funding UBI would require dismantling essential social programs or crippling the economy through excessive taxation. Furthermore, the claim that UBI fosters entrepreneurship ignores the real risk that a guaranteed income disincentivizes necessary labor, leading to widespread workforce shortages.",
