      "content": "The core argument against UBI is the predictable erosion of the work ethic, which is the engine of a functioning capitalist society. You can argue that providing an unconditional income removes the fundamental incentive for individuals to take on difficult, necessary, but low-paying jobs, leading to labor shortages in essential sectors like agriculture and service industries. This isn't just a theoretical risk; it's a direct threat to economic productivity, making the UBI proposal fiscally irresponsible and socially stagnant.",
      "source": "target",
